{"id":"en-184","title":"Maintain & Replace Beam Mirrors","family":"x-series","topic":"guides","read_minutes":1,"source_url":"https://wiki.1laser.com/en/x-series/maintain-replace-beam-mirrors","source_updated_at":"2026-03-02T09:16:21.228Z","body_html":"<div><h2 id=\"how-to-maintain-and-replace-beam-mirrors\"> How to Maintain and Replace Beam Mirrors</h2>\n<p>This guide explains how to properly maintain, clean, inspect, and replace beam mirrors in your laser machine. Regular mirror maintenance ensures optimal laser transmission efficiency, stable cutting power, and extended optical component lifespan.</p>\n<p>Neglecting beam mirror maintenance may lead to power loss, poor cutting performance, or optical damage.</p>\n<h2 id=\"required-tools\"> Required Tools</h2>\n<ul>\n  <li>M2, M3 hexagonal wrench</li>\n  <li>Lens cleaning solution</li>\n  <li>Dust-free swabs</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"operation-guide\"> <strong>Operation Guide</strong></h2>\n<h3 id=\"disassembly-of-the-chassis\"> Disassembly of the Chassis</h3>\n<p>Using an M2 Allen wrench, carefully remove the screws and place them uniformly, following the instructions in the pictures.</p>\n<figure><img src=\"https://zohodesk.1laser.com/galleryDocuments/edbsn418432b46744b98fb08560d2ef68457748c003c5d7961b4222e83dbe7de4c3d70912dbd60ddfe0ec3fffdf2894bf8429?inline=true\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\"></figure>\n<p>Using an M2 Allen wrench, carefully remove the screws and place them uniformly, following the instructions in the pictures.</p>\n<figure><img src=\"https://zohodesk.1laser.com/galleryDocuments/edbsn069574df96fc58ea8afa5e84588213b58cc0f94f0fd1ac7bf5fc2e93deb99b25c62db5127eeb36251d40f756810e5dbb?inline=true\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\"></figure>\n<figure><img src=\"https://zohodesk.1laser.com/galleryDocuments/edbsn418432b46744b98fb08560d2ef684577a1c0836b524d271c55550938926fa05ff6d4dad5304b3a966d64f06e5cfdd57d?inline=true\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\"></figure>\n<h3 id=\"locate-the-machines-beam-splitter\"> Locate the Machine&#x27;s Beam Splitter</h3>\n<figure><img src=\"https://zohodesk.1laser.com/galleryDocuments/edbsn069574df96fc58ea8afa5e84588213b5a3cf3bac92499d2c08f4393e784b3bf4e24b4d7a95a5749b78780785c20f7d2b?inline=true\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\"></figure>\n<figure><img src=\"https://zohodesk.1laser.com/galleryDocuments/edbsn9c6828f6122529b93e6f4a85e1eabaee6a73149b97dc029b670cb1bb26cdea4aa70575910657f321071a2b58e24ac80c?inline=true\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\"></figure>\n<h3 id=\"maintenance-cleaning-with-dust-free-swabs-and-lens-cleaning-solution\"> <strong>Maintenance Cleaning with Dust-free Swabs and Lens Cleaning Solution</strong>                                  </h3>\n<p>Use cleaning solution sprayed on swabs and gently wipe the front and back of the lens with a damp cotton swab.</p>\n<figure><img src=\"https://zohodesk.1laser.com/galleryDocuments/edbsn38c346ed9730b223ef917ec5ecddce7a425d277d35524ceb97a8fd324c4c9316bbe2956e4f76bb6068fecfdfdf6172d0?inline=true\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\"></figure>\n<figure><img src=\"https://zohodesk.1laser.com/galleryDocuments/edbsn7fcb121f1b08d077afd7688b757b8c08488949a6cd5b06e2b1d21a420c5c63ee4047c75ecb2dd68ce02c7aa923c083dd?inline=true\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\"></figure>\n<p> Use a dry cotton swab to clean the moisture from the lenses.</p>\n<figure><img src=\"https://zohodesk.1laser.com/galleryDocuments/edbsn8727a3b0b8522718bd76f7a91116e7933301c55516c15fc5cd18907e7015a9565d49bd0f961665f6eee54f171a8517d8?inline=true\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\"></figure>\n<h3 id=\"determining-if-a-lens-is-good-or-bad\"> <strong>Determining if a Lens is Good or Bad</strong></h3>\n<p>Look for scorched black marks on the lenses and try to clean them.</p>\n<figure>\n  <table>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr>\n        <td>\n          <figure><img src=\"https://zohodesk.1laser.com/galleryDocuments/edbsn7654805bff635cc5b5ef3dbe7b1b186d0ba760f7cdc99d5a5a50842cccb28d7dd7d402d2beaa6ae3cf61a096ecf40cfa?inline=true\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\"></figure>\n        </td>\n        <td>\n          <figure><img src=\"https://zohodesk.1laser.com/galleryDocuments/edbsnb00d69b22fe274ae5700c83fa5c7c3fc02171276147143603751fce2aa44f110b7144701b91adfbbac4f4d70d1c5598a?inline=true\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\"></figure>\n        </td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr>\n        <td>Normal lenses</td>\n        <td>Damaged lenses</td>\n      </tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</figure>\n<h3 id=\"replacement-of-combiner-lens\"> Replacement of Combiner Lens</h3>\n<p>Use an M3 Allen wrench to loosen the two screws on the side of the holographic mirror bracket.</p>\n<figure><img src=\"https://zohodesk.1laser.com/galleryDocuments/edbsn97c1dc924b394cf4401d210c872c0780d12b24ecd41ecf1046e8bd47600c787f9f9c2574a38bfaa4d16fecb5c92ed4a7?inline=true\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\"></figure>\n<p>Unscrew and remove the screws and place them uniformly, remove the lens.</p>\n<figure><img src=\"https://zohodesk.1laser.com/galleryDocuments/edbsn1b8b9514228616c810bc061cd62dac5c1b28be9c11ba718af16f7001f3db8fb09a7579719bfa9bf0ec5d752a7787ed73?inline=true\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\"></figure>\n<p>Reinstalling new lenses into the beam mirror holder.</p>\n<figure><img src=\"https://zohodesk.1laser.com/galleryDocuments/edbsn97c1dc924b394cf4401d210c872c07802787839601e9eeb6604880cd943094cf1eee0553c8a6d00216aa77b55aa7253c?inline=true\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\"></figure>\n<p> </p>\n<p><strong>Important Reminder:</strong></p>\n<p>If these steps do not resolve the issue, please submit a <a href=\"https://zohodesk.1laser.com/portal/en/newticket\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">support ticket</a>. A technician will then be able to conduct a more in-depth diagnosis.</p>\n</div>","headings":[{"level":1,"id":"how-to-maintain-and-replace-beam-mirrors","text":"How to Maintain and Replace Beam Mirrors"},{"level":2,"id":"required-tools","text":"Required Tools"},{"level":2,"id":"operation-guide","text":"Operation Guide"},{"level":3,"id":"disassembly-of-the-chassis","text":"Disassembly of the Chassis"},{"level":3,"id":"locate-the-machines-beam-splitter","text":"Locate the Machine's Beam Splitter"},{"level":3,"id":"maintenance-cleaning-with-dust-free-swabs-and-lens-cleaning-solution","text":"Maintenance Cleaning with Dust-free Swabs and Lens Cleaning Solution                                  "},{"level":3,"id":"determining-if-a-lens-is-good-or-bad","text":"Determining if a Lens is Good or Bad"},{"level":3,"id":"replacement-of-combiner-lens","text":"Replacement of Combiner Lens"}],"technical_version":"unknown"}